NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Form v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue\n3.6 is available as a release candidate but has not yet been released as\nstable. We hope it will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue 3.6 provides the component and composition behavior needed for Form\nComposition to work correctly and to preserve form and field types across\ntemplates and extracted components. Setting this minimum in v2 from the start\navoids introducing a breaking Vue version requirement later."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the Vue adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/vue-form","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-form","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useForm"},{"type":"text","value":" requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":". Their shape becomes the form's inferred\nvalue type."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    fullName: '',\n    age: 0,\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"fullName\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Full name</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).value)\"\n      />\n      <span v-for=\"error in field.errors\" :key=\"error.message\" role=\"alert\">\n        {{ error.message }}\n      </span>\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"age\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Age</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        type=\"number\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"\n          field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber)\n        \"\n      />\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Subscribe\n      :selector=\"(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const\"\n      v-slot=\"[canSubmit, isSubmitting]\"\n    >\n      <button type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!canSubmit || isSubmitting\">\n        {{ isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save' }}\n      </button>\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  </form>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The important pieces are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" define the complete initial value and drive type inference."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Field"},{"type":"text","value":" subscribes to one field. Its slot exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.value"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta"},{"type":"text","value":", and event handlers."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validators are ordered objects with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" function and explicit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" rerenders only its slot when the selected form state\nchanges."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates the form before calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"create-a-form","text":"Create a form","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you.\n\nThe Form v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue\n3.6 is available as a release candidate but has not yet been released as\nstable. We hope it will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable.\n\nVue 3.6 provides the component and composition behavior needed for Form\nComposition to work correctly and to preserve form and field types across\ntemplates and extracted components. Setting this minimum in v2 from the start\navoids introducing a breaking Vue version requirement later.\n\nInstall the Vue adapter:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-form\n```\n\n## Create a form\n\n`useForm` requires `defaultValues`. Their shape becomes the form's inferred\nvalue type.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    fullName: '',\n    age: 0,\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"fullName\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Full name</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).value)\"\n      />\n      <span v-for=\"error in field.errors\" :key=\"error.message\" role=\"alert\">\n        {{ error.message }}\n      </span>\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"age\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Age</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        type=\"number\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"\n          field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber)\n        \"\n      />\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Subscribe\n      :selector=\"(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const\"\n      v-slot=\"[canSubmit, isSubmitting]\"\n    >\n      <button type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!canSubmit || isSubmitting\">\n        {{ isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save' }}\n      </button>\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe important pieces are:\n\n- `defaultValues` define the complete initial value and drive type inference.\n- `form.Field` subscribes to one field. Its slot exposes `field.value`,\n  `field.meta`, and event handlers.\n- Validators are ordered objects with a `run` function and explicit\n  `triggers`.\n- `form.Subscribe` rerenders only its slot when the selected form state\n  changes.\n- `form.handleSubmit()` validates the form before calling `onSubmit`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nTanStack Form is a headless, type-safe form library. It owns form state and\nvalidation while leaving markup, styling, and component choice to you.\n\nThe Form v2 Vue adapter requires Vue 3.6 or newer. At the time of writing, Vue\n3.6 is available as a release candidate but has not yet been released as\nstable. We hope it will be stable by the time TanStack Form v2 becomes stable.\n\nVue 3.6 provides the component and composition behavior needed for Form\nComposition to work correctly and to preserve form and field types across\ntemplates and extracted components. Setting this minimum in v2 from the start\navoids introducing a breaking Vue version requirement later.\n\nInstall the Vue adapter:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-form\n```\n\n## Create a form\n\n`useForm` requires `defaultValues`. Their shape becomes the form's inferred\nvalue type.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useForm } from '@tanstack/vue-form'\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    fullName: '',\n    age: 0,\n  },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n    console.log(value)\n  },\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <form @submit.prevent=\"form.handleSubmit()\">\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"fullName\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value.trim() ? undefined : 'Enter your full name',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Full name</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).value)\"\n      />\n      <span v-for=\"error in field.errors\" :key=\"error.message\" role=\"alert\">\n        {{ error.message }}\n      </span>\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Field\n      name=\"age\"\n      :validators=\"[\n        {\n          triggers: ['change'],\n          run: ({ value }) =>\n            value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n        },\n      ]\"\n      v-slot=\"{ field }\"\n    >\n      <label :for=\"field.name\">Age</label>\n      <input\n        :id=\"field.name\"\n        :name=\"field.name\"\n        type=\"number\"\n        :value=\"field.value\"\n        :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n        @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n        @input=\"\n          field.handleChange(($event.target as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber)\n        \"\n      />\n    </form.Field>\n\n    <form.Subscribe\n      :selector=\"(state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const\"\n      v-slot=\"[canSubmit, isSubmitting]\"\n    >\n      <button type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!canSubmit || isSubmitting\">\n        {{ isSubmitting ? 'Saving…' : 'Save' }}\n      </button>\n    </form.Subscribe>\n  </form>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe important pieces are:\n\n- `defaultValues` define the complete initial value and drive type inference.\n- `form.Field` subscribes to one field. Its slot exposes `field.value`,\n  `field.meta`, and event handlers.\n- Validators are ordered objects with a `run` function and explicit\n  `triggers`.\n- `form.Subscribe` rerenders only its slot when the selected form state\n  changes.\n- `form.handleSubmit()` validates the form before calling `onSubmit`.\n"}
